# circleci_notification_integrations (Data Source)

Lists CircleCI notification integrations (Slack workspace installations, today).

## Availability

| | |
| --- | --- |
| **CircleCI Cloud** | Yes |
| **CircleCI Server** | No — served by the CircleCI v3 API, which a Server installation does not route to its public API service. Using this with `deployment = "server"` reports an explicit error rather than the confusing HTTP 404 the request would otherwise produce. |
| **API** | `GET /api/v3/notification/integrations` |
| **Organization type** | Any. |
| **Token** | Any valid API token with read access to the organization. |

## There is no resource to create an integration

A Slack workspace is installed through an OAuth flow in the CircleCI web UI, not through this API, so there is deliberately no `circleci_notification_integration` resource. Use this data source to discover the `id` of an integration installed that way, then manage whether it is active or disabled with `circleci_notification_integration_status`.

